type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Full change log:  [[https://kookma.github.io/TW-Shiraz/#ChangeLog]]

* ''3.1.1+nikorion'' -- 2026.10.12 -- `details` gets a dark bordered look by default (new `class` parameter; `faqs-details` keeps its own) and inline text passed as `src` no longer renders empty. With "Colorify UI buttons", the delete and move-to-trashbin buttons are red in view mode too, the edit toolbar traffic lights use saturated colours instead of pastels, and the Control Panel button stays violet while selected. `badge-pill` uses the Bootstrap 5 `rounded-pill` class. In `block` mode, alerts trim the outer margins of their first and last blocks (paragraph, list, table…), a leading heading keeping a little air above it.
* ''3.1.0+nikorion'' -- 2026.08.17 -- Full i18n rework, following the nikorion plugin convention. `tables/procs/lingo.tid` moved up to `language/lingo.tid` and its procedure was renamed `shiraz-tables-lingo` → `shiraz-lingo`, as it now covers the whole plugin; a `shiraz-lingo-text` function was added for attribute positions (`tooltip`, `aria-label`). Strings are split by domain under `language/<lang>/` (`common`, `settings`, `tables`) and now cover the Control Panel, the palette switcher, the dynamic-table UI and the search placeholders. `status` labels are translated while the stored field value stays canonical, custom values falling through unchanged. `readme`, `history` and `license` became language selectors; the licence body stays in English. Full French translation added.
* ''3.0.10'' -- 2025.07.07-- updated to TiddlyWiki 5.3.7
* ''3.0.0'' -- 2024.07.12 -- new Shiraz based on TiddlyWiki 5.3.5 and Bootstrap 5.33

---

''NOTE'': Shiraz 3.0.0 is a significant breakthrough and is not totally backward compatible. It uses Bootstrap 5.3.3, and TiddlyWiki 5.3.5 new features which is not found in earlier TiddlyWiki. It also uses new procedures with modified header.

